  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The volume charge density of a sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The number of lines of force per unit surface area coming out from the surface of the sphere is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>[Given : Permittivity of vacuum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "45",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.</p><p>Number&nbsp;of lines of force&nbsp;per unit area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> electric field at surface<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup